# File: tests/unit/pipeline/test_batch.py, tests/unit/test_unreal_retry.py, tests/unit/test_pie_preflight.py
# Generated from: specs/149-add-batch-finalize-with-lock-wait-unreal-mcp-timeout-retry-and-a-pie-preflight/requirements.md
Feature: Batch finalize with lock wait, Unreal MCP timeout retry, and a PIE preflight

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Batch finalize through the CLI
    Given three collections supplied as repeated --collection values or a --batch file
    When the developer runs the finalize command once
    Then the collections are finalized one at a time in the order given
    And the command exits after the last one finishes

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Batch finalize through the MCP tool
    Given finalize_asset is called with a list of requests
    When the batch runs
    Then get_finalize_job reports the running collection and completed out of total

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Per-asset result summary
    Given a batch in which one collection fails
    When the batch finishes
    Then every collection is listed with its state and the failure's code, message, and step
    And the CLI exits non-zero and prints the summary as JSON with --json

  @SCN004
  Scenario: One failed asset does not stop the batch
    Given a batch in which one collection fails
    When the batch runs without fail-fast
    Then the remaining collections are finalized
    And with fail-fast the remaining collections are skipped

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Wait for the lock instead of failing
    Given a finalize job holds the cache-root lock
    When a second finalize starts with the wait option
    Then it runs after the lock is released
    And with an expired wait limit it fails with finalize.job_running naming the holder job

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Default lock behavior is unchanged
    Given a finalize job holds the cache-root lock
    When a second finalize starts without the wait option
    Then it fails immediately with finalize.job_running

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Unreal MCP timeouts are retried with back-off
    Given the editor times out twice and then answers
    When import_ue runs
    Then it succeeds after increasing delays and records 3 attempts

  @SCN008
  Scenario: Retries are bounded
    Given the editor never answers
    When the retry limit is reached
    Then import_ue fails with import_ue.failed stating the attempts and total seconds waited

  @SCN009
  Scenario: A retry does not duplicate or corrupt an import
    Given an import timed out but the retry succeeds
    When the import finishes
    Then the result matches a single import with no duplicate assets and passing pivot checks

  @SCN010
  Scenario: PIE preflight before import
    Given the editor is in a PIE session
    When import_ue is about to start
    Then it waits for PIE to end before sending the import
    And at the wait limit or in refuse mode it fails with import_ue.editor_busy and sends no import

  @SCN011
  Scenario: Documentation
    Given the finalize MCP reference, the finalize-asset skill, and the MCP tool descriptions
    When a developer reads them
    Then they describe batch input, the summary, the wait option, the retry limits, and import_ue.editor_busy
